  x `zfs` is not a filesystem the installer formats
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:25:9]
 24 |     layout {
 25 |         filesystem "zfs"
    :         ^^^^^|^^^^
    :              `-- not a filesystem
 26 |         composefs #true
    `----
  help: the installer auto-partitions `xfs`, `ext4` and `btrfs`

  x `sealed` names no bootloader
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:10:5]
  9 | 
 10 |     layout {
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- no bootloader
 11 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
    `----
  help: no family answers the bootloader: `bootloader "grub2"` here, from what
        what the base component lists

  x `sealed` installs a sealed deployment onto xfs
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:10:5]
  9 | 
 10 |     layout {
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- xfs has no fs-verity
 11 |         filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
    `----
  help: the `debian` family installs with the composefs backend, which needs
        fs-verity: declare `ext4` or `btrfs`, or drop `filesystem` and take
        the family's own

  x `halfway` declares half an install layout
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/image.kdl:24:5]
 23 | 
 24 |     layout {
    :     ^^^|^^
    :        `-- no generic-image, admin-group, bootloader
 25 |         filesystem "zfs"
    `----
  help: nothing here has measured how `arch` installs, so this image answers
        for itself: a layout naming all of `filesystem`, `composefs`,
        `generic-image`, `admin-group` and `bootloader` builds install media,
        and no layout at all builds none
